My first ascension was genocideless; since then I make sure to genocide
at least mind flayers and liches.

Going wishless emphasises luck. I find that I use the castle's wand
mainly for magic markers, amulet of reflection, bag of holding, magical
armour (e. g., gauntlets of power, speed boots); sometimes also for
spellbooks. All of these items can be found or gained by polymorph. If in
your case "wishless" means, for example, "without a bag of holding" or
"without speed boots", the game becomes more difficult; if you would use
the wishes only to enchant your armour from +3 to +5, it's no big deal.

Or, in other terms: Genocides make the game easier because you remove
difficulties, wishes might make the game easier because you level the
influence of luck, so going genocideless is in general harder than going
wishless.

